{"name":"Ashley Blue","hex":"#8398a9","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ashley Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Oriana Small, known professionally as Ashley Blue, is an American pornographic film actress. She is a member of the AVN Hall of Fame, has hosted her own Vivid Radio show and written for Hustler magazine.\nIn 2011, she published a memoir of her career in the adult entertainment industry, titled Girlvert: A Porno Memoir."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Ashley_Blue_October_2005_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Ashley_Blue_October_2005_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashley_Blue","wikidata":"Q35728"},{"title":"Ashley (given name)","blocks":[{"text":"Ashley is a given name which was originally an Old English surname. It is derived from the Old English (Anglo-Saxon) words æsċ (ash) and lēah and translates to \"Dweller near the ash tree meadow\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashley_(given_name)","wikidata":"Q2655374"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/2010._%D0%94%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B5%D1%86%D0%BA._%D0%9A%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%BD%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B0%D0%BB_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%8C_%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%B0_010.jpg/500px-2010._%D0%94%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B5%D1%86%D0%BA._%D0%9A%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%BD%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B0%D0%BB_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%8C_%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%B0_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/2010._%D0%94%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B5%D1%86%D0%BA._%D0%9A%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%BD%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B0%D0%BB_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%8C_%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%B0_010.jpg/1280px-2010._%D0%94%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B5%D1%86%D0%BA._%D0%9A%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%BD%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B0%D0%BB_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%8C_%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%B0_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/2010._%D0%94%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B5%D1%86%D0%BA._%D0%9A%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%BD%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B0%D0%BB_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%8C_%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%B0_010.jpg/500px-2010._%D0%94%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B5%D1%86%D0%BA._%D0%9A%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%BD%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B0%D0%BB_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%8C_%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%B0_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.or